 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/en/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key to use for authenticating requests (mandatory).
+    # See https://console.scaleway.com/project/credentials
+  - secret_key: "..."
+
+    # project is the id of the Scaleway Project to discover Instances for.
+    # Either project or organization must be set.
+    #
+    # project: "..."
+
+    # organization is the id of the Scaleway Organization to discover Instances for.
+    # Either project or organization must be set.
+    #
+    # organization: "..."
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway zone to discover Instances in.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#regions-and-zones
+    #
+    # zone: "fr-par-1" | default "fr-par-1"
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: 80
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during relabeling:
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone the Instance is running in, e.g. `fr-par-1`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the state of the Instance, e.g. `running`, `stopped`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_commercial_type`: the commercial type (instance type) of the Instance, e.g. `DEV1-S`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ip`: the public IPv4 address of the Instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ip`: the private IPv4 address of the Instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma separated list of tags assigned to the Instance.
+
+By default, the discovered target address is set to the Instance public IP address if it has one, or to its private IP address otherwise. Instances without any IP address are skipped.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway Instance targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
